      {
        "id": "zimpol",
        "label": "SPHERE photograph",
        "thumbnail": "/scenes/athamantis/athamantis-zimpol-thumbnail.webp",
        "surface": "athamantis-zimpol-surface@2x.webp",
        "poles": "athamantis-zimpol-surface@2x.webp",
        "source": {
          "id": "athamantis-adam-shape",
          "path": "../manifest.json"
        },
        "falseColor": false,
        "noData": true,
        "notes": "14 deconvolved VLT/SPHERE/ZIMPOL frames, 2018-09-26 and 2018-09-28, cast onto the ADAM reconstruction from the same survey. The survey’s rotation record describes that frame, so the photograph rides it rather than the model the Shape view uses. Pointing and orientation are computed from that record, JPL Horizons geometry and each frame’s header, at the midpoint of its exposure; the disc centre is fitted to the limb of the mesh. With these cameras the mesh reproduces Vernazza et al. (2021) Figure B.38. Grayscale is photographed illumination and matched relative frame brightness. The deconvolution carries no radiometric calibration, so this is not measured albedo or colour. The grid marks surface that was unphotographed, too grazing, or rejected."
      }
    ]
